# Halt on a locked member

Locked types freeze **signatures** only: public, internal, and protected members (and Rust `pub` / `pub(crate)` / `pub(super)`). Body edits and private members on a locked type are allowed.

When a change needs a locked property, method, or constructor **signature** and that signature cannot be edited, stop. Tell the user which member is locked.

Do not work around the lock. Do not add a wrapper, a second field, a composed converter, or another path that carries the same data through an existing signature.
